  "decision_conditions": [
    "\r\n The applicant has failed to enter into a S106\r\n     agreement and therefore not in compliance with Policy 94 of the Local Plan Pt 1 (2024), specifically\r\n     in relation to the following planning obligations requirements (figures\r\n     applicable at the time of the assessment of the application):\r\n \r\n  Car Free Development - the\r\n      development is to be classified as car-free and residents will not be\r\n      eligible for parking permits. S278 works will be required upon completion\r\n      of the works relating to the development prior to occupation. An\r\n      application for Highway Works will be required.&nbsp;\r\n  Financial contribution of\r\n      £627.00&nbsp;towards the Epping Forest SAMMS\r\n  A S106 contribution of £250 would\r\n      be requested for CLP monitoring\r\n  A S106 request of £1000 is\r\n      requested toward improving sustainable modes of transport including\r\n      walking and cycling in the sites vicinity which will directly benefit new\r\n      residents in this development.\r\n \r\n\r\n",
    "\r\n The proposed development fails to provide a clear need\r\n     for a residential presence on a work site and fails to demonstrate or\r\n     justify the acceptability for a live/work unit within the trading estate\r\n     and its intended commercial use contrary to Policy 28 of the Local Plan Pt\r\n     1 (2024) and Policy E7 of the London Plan (2021).&nbsp;\r\n",
    "\r\n The proposed two storey extension by virtue of the\r\n     design and overall depth would result in a visually dominant addition due\r\n     to a lack of set back across the full width at the first and second floor\r\n     principle elevation. This development would be contrary to Policy 53 of\r\n     the Local Plan Pt 1 (2024).\r\n",
    "\r\n The proposed development fails to incorporate adequate\r\n     provision for refuse, recycling and food bins contrary to Policy 57 of the\r\n     Local Plan Pt 1 (2024).\r\n",
    "\r\n Due to the setback nature of the application site from\r\n     the public highway located within a commercial trading estate, the\r\n     proposal fails to demonstrate a safe or welcoming environment for\r\n     residents and\r\n     its unclear whether there will be any/ sufficient external lighting.\r\n     Therefore, the proposal in its current form could be detrimental to\r\n     pedestrian safety, as well as the well-being of future occupiers, contrary\r\n     to Policy 58 of the Local Plan Pt 1 (2024).\r\n",
    "Notwithstanding the\r\nearlier points of refusal, an Outline Construction Logistic Plan is required\r\nfor all new residential development, one has been provided. However, insufficient\r\ninformation has been provided. Outline CLP’s must be provided in relation to\r\nCLOCS guidance including template format which is available from the Councils\r\nHighways webpage https://www.walthamforest.gov.uk/parking-roads-and-travel/roads-and-pavements/highways-advice-developers/construction-logistics-plans.\r\nAs such, it is not possible to establish that the development complies with&nbsp;Policy 65 of the Local Plan Pt 1 (2024)."
  ],
